Z||000000||count_iblis||01-17-2001||10:06 AM||||I have a question.  As some of you know im getting a 3.1 dropped into my fiero.  Now the mechanic whom is doing this has had trouble finding one, well last week he found one and he has put it in.  I called today and he said that all that he was doing was rewiring the wiring and redoing the fuel line?  Now my question is this. How come he is doing this?  I thought everyone told me that this was a direct swap?  Could he have put in a alum. 3.1 head engine in?  Im confused,  can someone enlighten me?  <P><BR>Chris<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||01-17-2001||02:01 PM||||Did he re-use the Fiero intake manifold and fuel injection system or did he use the setup from the 3.1 engine?<P>I believe when people talk about not having to do much modification to install a 3.1 they are using the 3.1 long block with Fiero intake etc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||01-17-2001||05:35 PM||||Sounds to me like your mechanic is not using the fiero heads and induction system. You better find out!||||reg||1
Z||000003||count_iblis||01-17-2001||09:31 PM||||ok is this a bad thing?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-17-2001||09:42 PM||||If it is the 3.1 with aluminum heads and he actually gets it to run right you may have the only fiero with a 3.1-liter engine and aluminum heads. That would be awesome!<P>On the other hand it won't look like a fiero engine anymore.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||count_iblis||01-17-2001||09:45 PM||||well he said he had alot of modifications that needed to be done.  So i dont know.  I should have it tommorow or friday.  <P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||01-18-2001||12:24 AM||||From what I've heard, there's no way to use the Fiero manifold with aluminum heads.  If there was, it would be a <B>very</B> popular swap, because the alloy heads flow much better than the iron heads.<P>From the sounds of it, he swapped in the whole 3.1 setup.  It won't look stock, but you'll have a better engine overall... DIS ignition, better oiling system.  assuming it's a FWD 3.1.  If he used a RWD 3.1 it shouldn't be that much different..||||reg||
Z||000007||count_iblis||01-18-2001||08:04 AM||||well I just hope its the fwd. engine.  :+)<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||01-18-2001||05:20 PM||||Your right Standard but you can use the intake manifold that comes with the 3.1-liter engine instead of trying to adapt the 2.8 intake manifold right? Basically you are doing an engine swap were you use everything just like with the 3800 swap. ||||reg||1
