Z||000011||Hank is Here||01-19-2001||04:18 PM||||Count, <BR>Would like to hear more about this blunder by the mechanic.  keep us posted<P>------------------<BR>Hank is Here<BR>87 GT<BR>88 Coupe<BR>84 SE<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://a1060.g.akamai.net/f/1060/597/30minutes/www.zing.com/picture/p60e80970138058d8e3fae31692e151e0/fef43e85.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfiero||01-19-2001||04:25 PM||||The GTZ is a Chevy Beretta.  That was the last year for the Beretta and probably the best year too.  In '95 they went from a MPFI set-up to a SFI set-up, so your '96 engine will have sequential fuel injection on top of the aluminum heads, splayed valves, etc.<P>I'm not sure about horsepower numbers, but an ex girlfriend had/has a '95 Grand Am with this engine and it was pretty peppy......the 155 HP number sounds about right.<P>It's too bad you didn't know about this sooner.......you could have installed the 175-180 HP 3.4 from a '98 or newer Grand Am (looks identical to the 3.1 and has SFI too).  That would have given you another 25 or so horses.  Oh well.<BR> <BR>Let us know how things go.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 01-19-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000013||COUNTIBLIS||01-20-2001||10:16 AM||||I knew about the 3.4 but like I said the mechanic thought that it would be a hard swap????????!!!!!!!  Little did he know what he was getting into with this engine! The 3.4 would have been a breeze!  Oh well.  I still getting a better engine and all.  For now Im going to slap some Nos on there.  Then in a year I will go to a turbo.  <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||9
